```java
public class PowerOfThree {
    public boolean isPowerOfThree(int n) {
        if (n <= 0) {
            return false;
        }
        // 3^31 (2,147,483,647) is the largest power of 3 that can fit in a 32-bit signed integer
        if (n > 2147483647 / 3) {
            return false;
        }
        while (n % 3 == 0) {
            n /= 3;
        }
        return n == 1;
    }
}
```

This solution uses a while loop to repeatedly divide n by 3 until it becomes 1 or cannot be further divided by 3. If n is initially negative, we return false as a power of 3 cannot be negative. Additionally, we check if n is greater than the largest possible power of 3 (2,147,483,647 / 3) to avoid integer overflow. If n becomes 1 after division, it is a power of 3; otherwise, it is not. This solution has a time complexity of O(log n) and avoids loops/recursion.

